  <item>
    <title>Orville Peck – Mule</title>
    <link>https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/orville-peck-mule/</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="true">https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/orville-peck-mule/</guid>
    <pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 04:01:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <enclosure url="https://media.pitchfork.com/photos/6a62a500ee03086d8ecea647/16:9/w_1280,c_limit/Orville%20Peck%20-%20Mule.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/>
    <description><![CDATA[<p>The South African-born country singer’s latest album is a hell-and-back tale of addiction and redemption. But where other artists might opt for austerity, Peck goes all in on his usual pomp.</p>
<img src="https://media.pitchfork.com/photos/6a62a500ee03086d8ecea647/16:9/w_1280,c_limit/Orville%20Peck%20-%20Mule.jpeg" alt="Mule cover"/>
<img src="https://media.pitchfork.com/photos/6a62a500ee03086d8ecea647/16:9/w_1280,c_limit/Orville%20Peck%20-%20Mule.jpeg" alt="Mule cover"/>]]></description>
  </item>
